premise='Fixed defaultR/B8/nooverride; complete original W10/W11 meanings, explicitly separating an actual failed fleeing attempt(ret−1) from inability/cancelled forfeit(ret0). Valid ordinary battle objects, numeric bounds and candidates; UI/messages/callbacks preceding each named observation complete normally. Random statements are conditional on actually reaching each concrete random call; always-hit/blocked/zero-chance/partial-recalc alternatives do not invent a call. Same-round aggregate ordering is the actual observed call order, not a predetermined universal hit/effect/priority order. No runtime/random/model/native execution or allAI/MOVE/primary-domain certification.'
manual=[
 ('RC-RUN','pbRun60–159','Actual failed player wild fleeing calculation returns−1 and leaves decision0; successful normal escape writes decision3 and returns1. Trainer internalfalse accepted forfeit also writes3/returns1; declining it returns0.'),
 ('RC-RUN','pbRun60–159','Cannot attempt due to canRun/trapping/internal-trainer gates returns0. The runtime distinction is failed attempt versus unavailable/cancelled attempt, not a single falsey-success abstraction.'),
 ('R05','pbRun93–97','After any normal super return, recording writes[RUN,currentdecision] regardless of return−1/0/1; it then returns the exact super result. With initialdecision0, both failed attempt and cancelled forfeit therefore write[3,0].'),
 ('RC-COMMAND','RunMenu150–153/CommandLoop198–264','RunMenu returns pbRun!=0; actual command-loop Run branch stops remaining selections only if that is true. Thus ret−1 and1 stop, ret0 resumes selection and can later be overwritten by another successful registered command.'),
 ('R10','Organized40–144','Normal organized wrapper clears temporary record and retains a dump only for decision1/2/5; decision3 escape/forfeit does not retain it. These normal-return cleanup observations assume all preceding restoration/callbacks complete.'),
 ('RC-RUN','DebugRun28–52/pbRun69–71','Debug explicit outcomes write their chosen decisions and return1; cancelling debug outcome returns−1 without changing decision. This is distinct from declining ordinary facility forfeit and does not turn ret0 into failed fleeing.'),
 ('B17-BATTLE','pbRandom93','Ordinary Battle.pbRandom(x) directly calls global rand(x); the recording override interposes by normal Ruby dispatch on the actual battle receiver.'),
 ('RC-RAND','rand366–388','Top-level rand delegates Kernel.rand. The Kernel wrapper delegates single numeric to aliased oldRand(a), inclusive two-number/Range branches separately; only static valid positive integer domains are used here. Aliasing/native RNG return behavior is not executed.'),
 ('R05','Recording129–133/Playback188–192','Recording appends the returned Battle.pbRandom value after super completes, in call order; exception before return appends none. Playback reads sequence[randomindex] then increments, ignoring supplied bound and not calling live RNG.'),
 ('RC-REGMOVE','CalculatePriority136–262','fullCalc builds and shuffles randomOrder using Battle.pbRandom for every shuffle iteration before filtering missing battlers; equal priority/subpriority/speed is resolved by that stored tiebreaker. Partial recalculation reuses tiebreaker and does not repeat this shuffle.'),
 ('RC-TRY','SuccessPerHit532–581','Per-hit success reaches Move.pbAccuracyCheck only after charging/LockOn/override/invulnerability/skipAccuracy gates. Reaching that concrete method does not imply every always-hit branch draws.'),
 ('RC-USAGECALC','Accuracy87–124/Modifiers126–166','Normal non-always-hit accuracy after modifier callbacks calls actual Battle.pbRandom(100), then compares threshold and optional affection branch. Telekinesis/minimize/baseaccuracy0 or callback-set0 return before drawing.'),
 ('C-USE','ProcessMoveHit583–761','After actual damage/effect prefix, additional effect scans targets if user lacks active SheerForce, skips calcDamage0 or chance<=0, then compares Battle.pbRandom(100)<chance before pbAdditionalEffect. Chance100 still draws here; no blanket every effect draw guarantee.'),
 ('C-USE','ProcessMoveHit583–761','Flinch item/ability chance is a separate later Battle.pbRandom(100) call only for living target with nonzero calcDamage/no substitute/positive flinch chance. Its result is appended independently of accuracy/additional-effect draws.'),
 ('RC-AIUTIL','pbAIRandom5','AI.pbAIRandom calls global rand directly, not battle.pbRandom; recording wrapper does not append that draw.'),
 ('RC-AICHOOSE','whole393/Choose330–392','Ordinary AI final choice uses pbAIRandom(total_score) after threshold weights; bad-move switching tests use separate pbAIRandom100 gates. Score-dependent candidate selection is not recorded as RNG, while its eventual RegisterMove/Target results are recorded as commands.'),
 ('RC-AICHOOSE','GetMoveScore232–286/Against294–324','The complete central scoring bodies aggregate deterministic formulas and invoke named handler hooks; no standalone generic score-noise draw is added there. This finite observation does not certify every handler or transform all scoring-related calls into Battle.pbRandom.'),
 ('R03','PalaceAuto97–140/AIChooseSwitch195–235','Palace category/move sampling and HP-based switching use AI.pbAIRandom. They bypass recording RNG while successful actual chosen commands still go through recorded registration. These are own245 source facts, not inherited old interface FULL.'),
 ('RC-CATEGORY','ShellSideArm1112–1153','When its calculated physical/special damage ratios tie, this actual move calls global rand2 during command_phase and Battle.pbRandom2 outside it; unequal ratios select deterministically. The stage, not simply the method name, determines recording.'),
 ('RC-AIMOVE','rough_damage90–375','AI rough_damage invokes this move OnStartUse to calculate category for the named function; complete method contains no random damage-variance draw. Under command-phase evaluation its tied-category callback therefore uses the global branch, not the recording branch.'),
 ('RC-COMMAND','Command174–196','Normal command phase sets command_phase true through player and AI loops then false on normal exit (including nonzero decision early exit). This supplies the category callback phase distinction, without exception-safe reset guarantee.'),
 ('R05','PlaybackCommand198–222','Playback re-registers both recorded sides during player loop and returns immediately on AI loop, so ordinary live AI scoring/weighted-choice randomness is not rerun by that command path. Execution-stage Battle.pbRandom still consumes the saved sequence.'),
 ('RC-RUN','pbRun134–159','Normal escape chance specifically calls @battleAI.pbAIRandom256 when rate<256, and draws none when rate>=256 shortcircuits; this fleeing random is outside the recording RNG stream despite being mechanics-facing.')]
